0 FILE phasekeeper.ldr
0 Phasekeeper — equal-angle double-Cardan transmission
0 Name: phasekeeper.ldr
0 Author: CrispStrobe
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 !LICENSE BSD-3-Clause : see ../licenses/phasekeeper.txt
0 // Original double-Cardan layout, output tower, program and lessons by CrispStrobe.
0 // Flat base and motor-cradle pattern adapted from Brickwright Lite Quickstroke (BSD-3-Clause).
0 // One SPIKE angular motor on hub port A. Saved unwrapped encoder datum A=0 degrees.
0 // Program route: 0 -> 90 -> 180 -> 270 -> 360 -> 0 degrees.
0 // Manual/analytical envelope: -5 to 365 degrees; software bounds are not physical stops.
0 // U-joint centres: J1=(0,-30,0), J2=(120,-190,0) LDU; equal bend 36.869897646 degrees.
0 // Intermediate yoke fork axes are parallel to +Z; input/output shaft axes are parallel to world Y.
0 // Measure output angle on output_pointer about the output_axle axis relative to output_bearing_upper.
0 // Analytical 1:1 cancellation is ideal geometry, not a native-physics measurement.
0 // External standard LDraw meshes are referenced, not embedded. Connect motor cable to hub A.
